/* ============================================================================
binomial-to-normal-approximation.epher -- the continuity correction at work

Approximates the binomial probability P(X <= 55) for X with n = 100
trials and p = 0.5 by the normal with mean 50 and standard deviation
5, using the continuity correction: the binomial at 55 is matched by
the normal area up to 55.5, so the approximation is
normcdf((55.5 - 50) / 5). The rule of thumb says the normal is a good
stand-in when np and n(1 - p) are both at least 5, which holds here
with 50 and 50.

Run it from a terminal:
  Linux (deb, rpm):  epher /usr/lib/epher/scripts/statistics/distributions/binomial-to-normal-approximation.epher
  Windows:           epher "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\epher\scripts\statistics\distributions\binomial-to-normal-approximation.epher"
  macOS:             epher /Applications/epher.app/Contents/Resources/scripts/statistics/distributions/binomial-to-normal-approximation.epher
In the REPL:             load one of the paths above
Web/desktop:             paste the whole file into the entry, press Enter
Everything also works line by line in the TUI.

The knobs to edit are `n`, `p` and `k` below. Everything above the
results section is machinery you can leave alone.
============================================================================ */

// ---- the knobs -----------------------------------------------------------------
const n = 100    // trials of a fair coin
const p = 0.5    // success probability per trial
const k = 55     // the cut point: P(X <= k)

// ---- the exact binomial and the normal approximation --------------------------------
print("exact binomial P(X <= 55):", binomcdf(k, n, p))
print("normal approximation with correction:", normcdf((k + 0.5 - n * p) / sqrt(n * p * (1 - p))))
print("difference:", binomcdf(k, n, p) - normcdf((k + 0.5 - n * p) / sqrt(n * p * (1 - p))))

// ---- the parameters of the approximating normal ----------------------------------------
print("mean n * p:", n * p)
print("stdev sqrt(n * p * (1 - p)):", sqrt(n * p * (1 - p)))

/* ---- expected output ----
= 100
= 0.5
= 55
= exact binomial P(X <= 55): 0.864373487962
= normal approximation with correction: 0.864333939054
= difference: 0.0000395489088035
= mean n * p: 50
= stdev sqrt(n * p * (1 - p)): 5
*/